      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Regnard et al.",
        "AbstractText": "Bos taurus papillomaviruses infect cattle, which has both animal health and economic consequences. This is the first report and sequence of Bos taurus papillomavirus type 1 isolated from warts in cattle in Morocco. The double-stranded DNA (dsDNA) genome was 7,945 bp in size, and eight open reading frames were identified."
      },
